#
# The image `cpp-interface-standard` runs in, wherever it runs: the hosted lane,
# a build machine judging an update to main, a workstation. `scripts/gate`
# builds it (tagged by this file's digest) and runs `scripts/gate
# cpp-interface-standard` inside it with the checkout mounted at its own path
# ("Gates that run in an image" in tools/git-hooks/gate_registry.py).
#
# ## Why GCC 15, pinned
#
# The defect that started the gate was a transitive include: a public header
# named `uint64_t` without `<cstdint>`, and GCC 15's libstdc++ stopped providing
# `<cstdint>` through `<string>` at C++17 while still doing so at C++20. The
# newest libstdc++ is the one that drops such includes first, so the gate runs
# the newest GCC, pinned so that a new release moves the measurement only when
# someone moves the pin. The image is Debian with GCC 15 in /usr/local.
#
# ## What the configure needs beside it
#
# CMake and Ninja, Python for the tool and the tests' CMake, git for the
# submodules, and the development packages cpp-httplib (TLS, zlib, brotli) and
# the GLib dispatcher link against. `sce-codegen`, which the runner builds in
# here before the gate, needs libxml2 (the `libxml` crate behind its XSD
# validator) and libclang (that crate's bindgen): measured on the lane's second
# run, `Unable to find libclang`.
#
# `sce-codegen` formats the C++ it writes with clang-format of major 19 and
# refuses without it (docs/SCE_CODEGEN_DETERMINISM.md). The image's Debian
# release decides which clang-format its archive carries, so the pinned major
# comes from the wheel instead, which is the same on any base.
#
# ## Rust
#
# None is installed here, and no gate installs one (scripts/lib/rust_toolchains.sh).
# The runner outside mounts the toolchain it selected, read-only, where the
# runner inside looks for a declared release (`~/.local/rust/<release>`), and
# names that release with `--rust`: the pinned release a build machine carries
# as a bx tool, or the one the hosted lane installed. The gate in the image
# therefore builds with the release the plan named and no other. A generator
# linked in this image is not one to hand to another libc, or back, so its
# build directory and cargo's registry are a cache of the image's own.
#
# The mesh SDKs are not installed: their targets are then not configured, and a
# header that needs one of them is reported by name as NOT MEASURED, which is
# neither a pass nor a failure. The floors the gate holds are set below what
# such an image measures.
FROM gcc:15.3.0

RUN apt-get update \
    && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \
        cmake \
        ninja-build \
        python3 \
        python3-venv \
        pkg-config \
        git \
        ca-certificates \
        libssl-dev \
        zlib1g-dev \
        libbrotli-dev \
        libglib2.0-dev \
        libxml2-dev \
        libclang-dev \
    && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*

RUN python3 -m venv /opt/clang-format-19 \
    && /opt/clang-format-19/bin/pip install --no-cache-dir clang-format==19.1.7

ENV PATH=/opt/clang-format-19/bin:$PATH \
    CC=gcc \
    CXX=g++
